From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:34:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/28] Add Label, Section, Form, Stepper, lazy stacks and
 NavigationView

None of these existed. They are made of SwiftUI parts with iOS's default look.
Form puts its sections in white rounded cards on the grouped background, with
separators between rows, uppercase headers and footers; rows outside a
section get a card of their own. Sections in a list lay out their own rows,
which a trait tells List. Stepper draws UIStepper's two buttons and stops at
its bounds. Label shows its icon and title, or one of them with labelStyle.
LazyVStack and LazyHStack make every child at once. NavigationView is a
NavigationStack, as on iPhone, and NavigationLink also takes its destination
as a view, as before iOS 16.
